    "explanation": "This ruling addresses both parties. The driver's account of the trip is largely borne out by the platform's own data, and he is not criticised for his arrival or his wait: he tapped 'arrived' at 19:24:52, the GPS trace places him inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius from the very first in-geofence fix (dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0, so the marker was true and POL-NS-05 does not fire), and he held position for a continuous 471 seconds across 47 consecutive qualifying fixes — 2.6 times the 180-second free waiting period in force for this trip — before cancelling at 19:32:46 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the codes POL-NS-01(d) recognises. POL-NS-01 limbs (a) to (d) are therefore satisfied and POL-NS-06 reports no waiting-period shortfall (shortfall_sec -291). The driver's SGD 3.60 figure (0.80 x SGD 4.50) is not disputed as arithmetic.\n\nNevertheless the SGD 4.50 cancellation_fee does not stand, because POL-NS-04 displaces POL-NS-01, and POL-NS-01 itself makes the fee chargeable only where no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the conditions. All three limbs of POL-NS-04 hold on this record. (a) During the waiting window the rider sent, at 19:25:22, 'im at the pickup, which car are you? i cant see you' — a statement of his own position, a request for the driver's position and a statement that he could not see the vehicle, each of which the clause names as locating or coordinating content — followed by 'hello? are you here' at 19:27:22. (b) The chat log contains no driver message at all, both rider messages carry null read timestamps, and trip_record.in_app_calls is empty, so the driver neither replied within 120 seconds nor placed an in-app call before terminating the trip. (c) The rider's own track carries 85 qualifying fixes (85 of 85 pass the accuracy filter) and every one lies within 12.1 m of the pickup pin (mean 8.1 m, minimum 4.3 m), far inside the 150 m rider-presence radius set for a LARGE_VENUE zone, with the track running 19:21:39 to 19:34:19 and so covering the whole waiting window.\n\nThe driver's answer to limb (c) — that a whole-track count does not show presence across the waiting window — does not succeed: because the furthest of the 85 fixes is 12.1 m from the pin, any subset of the track, including the waiting window itself, is inside the radius, so the test is affirmatively satisfied and not merely undecidable (POL-NS-11 therefore does not engage). His wider point that the pickup failed at boarding rather than at arrival is exactly what the clause addresses: a rider standing within 12 m of the pin who messages twice and receives no reply, no read receipt and no call has done what POL-NS-04 asks of him, and the clause exonerates him. The counterparty statement 'I waited the full time' answers only the dwell question, which is not the defect raised, and does not meet limb (b)'s silence.\n\nBecause POL-NS-04 grants the refund with no driver compensation payable, the driver's claim to SGD 3.60 fails: POL-NS-07 compensates only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and POL-NS-04 does displace it. The cancellation_fee line of SGD 4.50, shown as CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, is returned to the rider in full; the driver receives no payout and the platform retains nothing from a fee that was never chargeable.\n\nOn escalation, both sides agree and the record confirms no trigger: rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d are both 0, rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1 (below the 3 POL-NS-09(d) names), and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip — 2 no-show terminations in 30 days against 58 completed trips is a rate of 0.034, below the 0.08 rate and below the count of 4. Only driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d and driver_profile.completed_trips_30d are citable for that test, and the lifetime prior_no_show_flags counter was correctly not used as a ground. No artifact carrying a deciding fact is impaired: the trip record, GPS trace, chat log and fare breakdown are each COMPLETE at weight 1.0 with no issue codes, so nothing is down-weighted. The MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02716-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, no payload) carries no fact for either side: the dwell was a single continuous in-geofence run, so POL-NS-06(i) never came into play. Confidence is 0.9, within the cap of 1.0 set by the weight of the artifacts that carry the deciding facts (chat log, trip record and GPS trace, each at 1.0), and above the 0.70 floor. No referral is ordered, because no clause produces one on these facts."
